# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Mirror + resume.md — environment
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. With NO keys set, the app runs in demo mode:
# it serves the seeded example candidate + a captured before/after, clearly
# labeled as seeded (never passed off as live).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- The model queried in the Mirror (Perplexity only in this prototype) ---
# Get a key at https://www.perplexity.ai/settings/api
PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides (sensible defaults used if unset):
# PERPLEXITY_MODEL=sonar            # or sonar-pro
# PERPLEXITY_ENDPOINT=https://api.perplexity.ai/chat/completions

# --- The judge (verdict strips). A small model, temp 0. Provider-agnostic. ---
# JUDGE_PROVIDER: anthropic | openai | perplexity   (default: anthropic)
JUDGE_PROVIDER=anthropic
# For anthropic:
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# JUDGE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com
#
# For openai (or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint):
# JUDGE_API_KEY=
# JUDGE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
#
# If no judge key is set, verdicts fall back to a deterministic heuristic and
# are flagged best-effort in the UI.

# --- Durable, private storage (recommended for any real deployment) ---------
# Connect a Vercel KV / Upstash Redis store to the project and these are
# injected automatically. Without them the app falls back to local disk (./data)
# or, on Vercel, ephemeral /tmp (generated profiles won't survive restarts).
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# (UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN are also accepted.)

# --- Beta cost + abuse guardrails -------------------------------------------
# Caps only apply to LIVE model calls; cached/seeded reads are always free.
# MAX_LIVE_QUERIES_PER_DAY=500
# MAX_LIVE_QUERIES_PER_MINUTE_PER_IP=12

# --- Public URL of THIS app (the placeholder host for profile pages) --------
# The hosted profile at /{slug} must be a REAL, fetchable URL for the
# before/after to work. In local dev this defaults to the request host. For a
# demo, set this to your public deploy or tunnel origin (no trailing slash),
# then re-run `npm run seed` so seeded answers reference the right URL.
# APP_URL=https://your-app.example.com
